    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Right unit.** National-length validation belongs to `TelephoneNormalizer`, the existing home of E.164 parsing/validation. The new check is threaded into `toE164` right after the existing digit-count bound, which is the natural place for it.\n- **Additive, not catch-all.** The class still does one thing (normalize/validate into E.164). The new concern is expressed as a single focused private helper (`hasValidNationalLength`) plus one lookup constant, rather than inflating an existing method with inline logic.\n- **No duplication.** The country-code-to-length mapping is centralized in one `Map` constant, and the min/max bounds continue to reuse the existing `MIN_DIGITS`/`MAX_DIGITS` fields rather than reintroducing magic numbers.\n- **Idiomatic.** `private static final Map.of(...)` for a fixed lookup table, a small well-named boolean helper, Javadoc consistent in tone/placement with the existing class docs, and the error message updated in step with the new rule \u2014 all match the surrounding conventions.\n\nA maintainer of this repo would find the placement and shape natural.",
